      ],
      "source": "https://pennsylvaniainfo.blog/worcester-pennsylvania-ultimate-guide",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally inhabited by the Lenni Lenape Native Americans, the land that would become Worcester saw an influx of Welsh and German immigrants seeking religious freedom and economic opportunity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://pennsylvaniainfo.blog/worcester-pennsylvania-ultimate-guide",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Worcester Porcelain Museum preserves this rich heritage and promotes appreciation for the town’s contributions to the porcelain industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
